e the following:\\n{\\\"query\\\":{\\\"range\\\":{\\\"response\\\":{\\\"gt\\\":\\\"499\\\",\\\"lt\\\":\\\"600\\\"}}}\\n\\nOr should I use a match query against response.keyword? The response field is a string (probably a keyword with no text subfield). Actually, the field list shows \\\"response\\\":\\\"string\\\" and \\\"response.keyword\\\":\\\"string\\\". Hmm, both are listed. If response is analyzed as text, match queries would work per-token. A range query on an analyzed field... In ES, range queries on text fields are possible (they compare against the analyzed terms). If all values are single tokens, it should work fine.\\n\\nAs an alternative, a simpler and more robust approach: use a terms query matching all possible 5xx codes: 500, 501, 502, 503, 504, 505, 508, 510, 511, 516, 520, 521, 522, 523, 524, 525, 526, 529, 530, 535, 598, 599. That's too many.\\n\\nI'll go with the range query: {\\\"query\\\":{\\\"range\\\":{\\\"response\\\":{\\\"gte\\\":\\\"500\\\",\\\"lte\\\":\\\"599\\\"}}}}. Lexicographic: \\\"500\\\" <= x <= \\\"599\\\" — this correctly captures all 3-digit codes 500–599. Good.\\n\\nThe schedule_interval is \\\"1m\\\" (check every minute).\\n\\nThe rule is created disabled by default — the tool description says \\\"Created DISABLED by default — call enable_alert_rule to start it.\\\" So, I'll create it and then enable it.\\n\\nAlright, let's create the rule.\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"Dashboard created. Now creating the alert rule for 5xx errors.\\n\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"create_alert_rule\", \"arguments\": {\"name\": \"LOC-cdcde024 5xx errors\", \"rule_type_id\": \".es-query\", \"consumer\": \"stackAlerts\", \"params\": {\"searchType\": \"esQuery\", \"esQuery\": \"{\\\"query\\\":{\\\"range\\\":{\\\"response\\\":{\\\"gte\\\":\\\"500\\\",\\\"lte\\\":\\\"599\\\"}}}}\", \"index\": [\"kibana_sample_data_logs\"], \"timeField\": \"timestamp\", \"threshold\": [10], \"thresholdComparator\": \">\", \"timeWindowSi